            "question": "How do Dreamtape Nose Strips work?",
            "answer": "<p>Each strip has a flexible spring band that sits across the bridge of your nose. As it tries to straighten back out, it gently lifts the sides of your nose open, widening the nasal passage underneath. That means less resistance on every breath, so air moves more easily even if you're a little congested. There's nothing medicated about it — the effect is purely mechanical, and it starts the moment you put one on.</p>"
          }
        },
